{
  "id": "oscillatory-interference-model",
  "term": "oscillatory interference model",
  "definition": "An oscillatory interference model is a biological model of grid cell firing that explains the hexagonal spatial firing pattern as arising from interference among multiple oscillators. In this model, noise can cause drift in the position signal over time, with greater stability when more oscillators are involved.",
